  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}(1+9{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{(1+(3x)^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(3x)]_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{\\pi }{12y}]}_{1/3}^{1/4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}}+\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
